  "id": "COMPOUND:22609 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "NRF2 activator Geopyxin F appears to have a direct target relationship with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of intermediate molecules, all of which are targets of SNU-387. This suggests that Geopyxin F may act through a pathway where it activates SNU-387, which in turn targets multiple downstream proteins, including Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The evidence indicates that Geopyxin F may influence the activity of SNU-387, which is a key player in the regulation of viral replication, as it is involved in the targeting of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The presence of multiple distinct targets of SNU-387 implies that the interaction between Geopyxin F and SNU-387 may be a critical step in the mechanism by which the NRF2 activator exerts its effect on the replicase polyprotein. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the interaction between Geopyxin F and Replicase polyprotein 1ab.",
